---
// /en/privacy/ (создана 2026-07-12): адаптация RU /privacy/.
// ДРАФТ - юридическую формулировку при необходимости сверить со специалистом.
import Page from '../../../layouts/Page.astro';
import { site } from '../../../data/site';
---

<Page
  title="Privacy · Valeriy Karasaev"
  description="What data karasaev.com collects, and what happens to the information you share when booking and working with me."
  lang="en"
  translation="/privacy/"
  hideCta={true}
>
  <div class="page-head">
    <div class="kicker">Privacy</div>
    <h1 class="page-title">What happens to your data</h1>
    <p class="lead">In short: this site collects almost nothing about you. And what you tell me personally is protected by professional ethics.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="meta-line"><span class="meta-num">01</span><span class="meta-label">The website</span></div>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      karasaev.com is a static website. It doesn't use cookies, doesn't show ads and contains
      no social media trackers. Forms on the site don't collect data: all communication goes
      directly through Telegram or email. Fonts are loaded from Google Fonts - when a page loads,
      your browser contacts Google's servers under their rules.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="meta-line"><span class="meta-num">02</span><span class="meta-label">Booking and correspondence</span></div>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      When you write to me on Telegram or by email, I receive what you sent: your name, contact
      and the text of your message. I use this data only to get in touch with you and organize
      our work. I don't pass it to third parties and don't use it for mailings without your consent.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="meta-line"><span class="meta-num">03</span><span class="meta-label">Therapy</span></div>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Everything said in sessions is confidential. Two exceptions: supervision (discussing the work
      without names or identifying details - a professional standard) and a direct threat to life.
      Details are in the <a href="/docs/working-rules-en.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">working rules (PDF)</a>
      and on the <a href="/en/principles/">Working Principles</a> page.
    </p>
    <p>Questions about data: <a href={'mailto:' + site.email}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Page>
